[114.738353, "o", "BUG FIX SUMMARY - filter_logs.py\r\n=================================\r\n\r\nProblem:\r\n--------\r\nThe script was flagging ~4000 requests as slow when only ~200 were actually slow.\r\n\r\nRoot Cause:\r\n-----------\r\nThe regex pattern 'response_time=(\\d+)ms' was matching 'upstream_response_time=XXXms'\r\nbecause it didn't prevent substring matches. The pattern matched the substring\r\n'response_time=XXXms' within 'upstream_response_time=XXXms'.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, the production logs use TWO formats:\r\n1. response_time=XXXms (with ms suffix)\r\n"]
[114.738398, "o", "2. response_time_ms=XXX (without ms suffix)\r\n\r\nThe original pattern only handled format #1.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\n---------\r\nUpdated the regex patterns to:\r\n1. Use negative lookbehind: (?<!upstream_)response_time=(\\d+)ms\r\n2. Handle both formats with two patterns\r\n3. This prevents matching upstream_response_time while catching both formats\r\n\r\nResults:\r\n--------\r\nBefore: 1325 requests flagged (mostly false positives from upstream times)\r\nAfter: 187 requests flagged (actual slow requests >500ms)\r\n\r\nBackup saved to: filter_logs.py.bak\r\n"]
[114.738514, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[114.738556, "o", "user@1588c03b0353:~/perf$ "]
